// `@require(&t, c)` is `@expect`'s check, and the test ends there if c doesn't hold: its line
// says `required:`, an earlier failure of the test is still shown, and nothing after it
// runs, not the test's next lines, not a `defer`, also when a fn the test calls requires.
// The test is one failed test, and the others run. One that holds is a check as any.
//# $ ctxc test .
//# exit: 1
//# stdout:
//| ./t.ctx:20: fail: the_test_goes_on_after_one_that_holds: found[0].name == "carth": bastila == carth
//| written before
//| ./t.ctx:27: fail: the_test_ends_at_one_that_does_not: found.len == 2: 0 == 2
//| ./t.ctx:28: fail: the_test_ends_at_one_that_does_not: required: found.len > 0: 0 > 0
//| ./t.ctx:34: fail: a_condition_that_is_no_comparison: required: some{ n = 0 }
//| ./t.ctx:8: fail: in_a_fn_the_test_calls: required: rows{ n }.len > 0: 0 > 0
//| tests: 6 run, 2 passed, 4 failed, 0 skipped, 0 not selected, 10 checks
//# $ ctxc test . -v holds after
//# exit: 1
//# stdout:
//| ./t.ctx:12: pass: a_require_that_holds_is_a_check
//| ./t.ctx:20: fail: the_test_goes_on_after_one_that_holds: found[0].name == "carth": bastila == carth
//| ./t.ctx:44: pass: the_tests_after_it_run
